2f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-317652/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317652" :question/id #uuid "4cadee86-2a70-5613-ad3c-bf59bc4d8e2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-317652" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨5,-3,4⟩$ and $b=⟨1,2,-2⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5-6-8}{1+4+4}\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{9}\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317652/field-1" "q-317652/field-2" "q-317652/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
